    "project": {
      "accession": "PXD056683",
      "title": "pig liver proteomics of N-glycosylation modification",
      "additionalAttributes": [],
      "projectDescription": "This research investigated the proteomics of total proteins and N-glycosylation modification from groups between Wuzhishan and Large White pigs at 4-month-old, and Wuzhishan pigs at 4-month-old and 8-month-old.",
      "sampleProcessingProtocol": "The 6 Wuzhishan pigs of 4-month-old (1 boar and 2 sows) and 8-month-old (1 boar and 2 sows), and 3 Large White pigs of 4-month-old (1 boar and 2 sows) were feeding in a similar environment with free food and water for a week before slaughtering. After one week, all he pigs withdrawn feed for 24h, and stunned via electric shock, and the liver tissue were collected and frozen directly in liquid nitrogen.",
      "dataProcessingProtocol": "Peptide preparation:ground to powder and extracted total protein by kit (Thermo Scientific T-PER, 78510). glycopeptides preparation:the peptides were dissolved in enriched buffer,and centrifuged and collected, and then digested by PNGase F glycosidase.",
